    "content": "The Saturday Night Live Five-Timers Club is an exclusive group of hosts who have helmed the show at least five times, traditionally celebrated with a smoking jacket. Established on-screen in 1990 by Tom Hanks, the concept honors frequent hosts, with Buck Henry being the first to actually hit five, and many others joining later. Key Members & Highlights: Most Hosted: Alec Baldwin holds the record with 17 hosting appearances, followed by Steve Martin with 16. Notable Members: Tom Hanks, Tina Fey, Scarlett Johansson, John Goodman, Drew Barrymore, Melissa McCarthy, Will Ferrell, Paul Rudd, Ben Affleck, and John Mulaney. First Female Member: Candice Bergen. The Sketch: The club is often featured in monologues where members show their IDs, wear smoking jackets, and interact in a luxurious, secret lounge. Watch Emma Stone's induction into the exclusive Five-Timers Club:51sEntertainment TonightYouTube• Dec 3, 2023 51s Recent Inductees:John Mulaney became a member in 2022, and Jack Black joined the prestigious ranks in April 2026, as noted in the Today.com video. Today.com video",
